   {
    "question": "What do the dVRK threads say about tracking errors on a PSM?",
    "asked_by": "sup.wong",
    "status": "completed",
    "stop_reason": "final_answer",
    "tools": [
     {
      "tool": "search_threads",
      "ok": true,
      "error_kind": null
     }
    ],
    "tools_called": [
     "search_threads"
    ],
    "approvals": [],
    "answer": "The dVRK threads mention tracking errors on a PSM (Patient-Side Manipulator) in the following context:\n\n1. In thread [sawIntuitiveResearchKit/26#q](thread:sawIntuitiveResearchKit/26#q), there is a discussion about using better PID (Proportional-Integral-Derivative) tracking errors on the PSM for the last 4 joints. The current implementation has large PID tracking errors, which are attributed to the lack of trajectory generation during the engage procedure of the tool and adapter. A temporary fix involves adding an extra step after the engage procedure to allow time for the PID command to finish before adjusting the PID tracking tolerance to a more reasonable number (10) [thread:sawIntuitiveResearchKit/26#q].\n\n2. In thread [sawIntuitiveResearchKit/26#a](thread:sawIntuitiveResearchKit/26#a), a partial fix is mentioned in a specific commit (8571756209bba957f58d45d85589700d70a756fd) in the devel branch. However, the fix is described as partial because the tracking errors were still large, and there is a suggestion to increase the PID gains, although this is not done immediately due to hardware concerns [thread:sawIntuitiveResearchKit/26#a].\n\n3. In thread [sawIntuitiveResearchKit/4#a](thread:sawIntuitiveResearchKit/4#a), there is a reference to the need for a trajectory generator to allow tighter PID tracking tolerance and potentially address encoder discrepancies. This is linked to the issue mentioned in thread #26 [thread:sawIntuitiveResearchKit/4#a].\n\nThese threads highlight ongoing efforts to improve the PID tracking errors on the PSM, with some fixes implemented and others still under consideration or development.",
    "model_calls": 3,
    "tokens": 6833,
    "seconds": 11.4,
    "guard_repairs": 1,
